  "body": {
    "id": "lem:certified-global-identification",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "If \\(\\mathfrak C(\\Xi)\\) returns \\(\\mathtt{CERTIFIED}\\), its recorded valid cover \\(\\mathscr C\\) satisfies \\(\\mu_{\\mathcal T}(r_{\\mathrm{id}};\\mathscr C)\\geq\\underline\\mu_{\\mathcal T}>0\\), so every same-graph pair closer than \\(r_{\\mathrm{id}}\\) is separated in a co-containing chart. Every feasible pair at least \\(r_{\\mathrm{id}}\\) apart has squared \\(W\\)-distance at least \\(\\underline\\Lambda_{\\mathcal T}>0\\), with the remote claim vacuous when that pair set is empty. Therefore every \\(m_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}\\) is globally injective on \\(\\Theta_{\\boldsymbol d}\\), and \\(Q_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\cdot;m_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\theta_0))\\) has unique minimum \\(\\theta_0\\) with the certified remote separation outside its local neighborhood.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "certificate-output",
      "certificate-status",
      "moment-map",
      "graph-parameter-space",
      "injectivity-radius",
      "certified-local-injectivity-bound",
      "chart-projection-cover",
      "projected-moment-map",
      "certified-remote-bound",
      "weight",
      "score",
      "true-parameter",
      "cpcm-graph",
      "moment-grid"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:certificate-procedure",
      "def:grid-criterion"
    ],
    "justification": "This prevents local Jacobian rank from substituting for global uniqueness.",
    "gap": "A local inverse theorem alone does not certify a unique compact-box population minimum.",
    "consumer": "It supplies the global identification premise for the deterministic minimum-distance estimator.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(\\theta,\\theta'\\in\\Theta_{\\boldsymbol d}\\) have equal moment vectors.  If\n\\(\\|\\theta-\\theta'\\|_2<r_{\\mathrm{id}}\\), validity of the recorded cover puts them in a common chart \\(C_{\\boldsymbol d c}\\).  Equality of moment vectors implies equality after projection, and hence\n\\[\n0=\\langle\\phi_{\\boldsymbol d c}(\\theta)\n-\\phi_{\\boldsymbol d c}(\\theta'),\\theta-\\theta'\\rangle\n\\geq\\underline\\mu_{\\mathcal T}\\|\\theta-\\theta'\\|_2^2.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\underline\\mu_{\\mathcal T}>0\\), this forces \\(\\theta=\\theta'\\).  If instead their distance is at least \\(r_{\\mathrm{id}}\\), the certified remote bound gives\n\\[\n\\|m_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\theta)\n-m_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\theta')\\|_W^2\n\\geq\\underline\\Lambda_{\\mathcal T}>0,\n\\]\ncontradicting equality.  When the remote set is empty this second case cannot occur.  Thus the moment map is globally injective.\n\nFor \\(g_0=m_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\theta_0)\\), positive definiteness of \\(W\\) gives\n\\[\nQ_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\theta;g_0)=0\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\nm_{\\boldsymbol d,\\mathcal T}(\\theta)=g_0\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\theta=\\theta_0.\n\\]\nThe displayed remote bound supplies the asserted quantitative separation outside the local neighborhood.",
